{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"Correction to prior shell-mangled selectors: all 5 final oracle nodes were observed RED before production edits. A separate standard-tier implementer saw only the primary test and completed in one attempt. Restored edge, close-path, and doc tests pass; focused caused_by suite is 14 of 14 green; exact acceptance selectors in tests/unit/metrics/test_blame.py for distinguishes and partial_failure pass; lint and typecheck pass. Mutation treating failed blame as successful-empty made both partial-failure unit and real close-path tests fail, proving the guard prevents an incorrect persisted caused_by link."},"env_id":"ade0f2ef-51cc-45a2-bb97-c09846cd3df5","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1785622302031126001,"uuid":"c7a37e72-1d02-4ad6-868c-9fc9d46616c9"}